& [SourcePrompt: IR2FinalSlices] is the preserved source for minting IR2 final slices
  + [source_kind] is manager-derived implementation-readiness slice source
  + [origin] is accepted IR1 implementation substrate pack and reviewed inert scaffold creation
  + [purpose] is split IR2 authority-file parser and SQLite projection builder into clean final slices before parser or projection implementation begins
  + [chunk_ref] is IR2 authority-file parser and SQLite projection builder
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: create an IR2 final slice surface that can be executed without depending on unsliced downstream chunks
  = must: preserve SOP files as authority and SQLite as a rebuildable derived projection
  = must: define parser and projection behavior before implementing parser or SQLite builder code
  = must: define source artifact discovery, parser profile, KernelRecord extraction mapping, hash ledger validation, and stale projection handling
  = must: define SQLite projection schema and rebuild policy before creating database-writing code
  = must: define fixtures and expected-output ledgers before accepting parser/projection implementation
  = must: require completion review after every IR2 slice
  = must: keep LangGraph runtime implementation, surface implementation, adapter implementation, operations simulator implementation, operations control, and live machine control out of IR2
  = must: keep generated SQLite files, caches, indexes, and extracted projections non-authoritative
  = must: preserve no live operations control authorized

& [RequiredIR2SliceSet] is the source-level slice set for IR2
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S01 parser and projection boundary and invariant map
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S02 SOP artifact discovery and parser profile contract
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S03 KernelRecord extraction and validation mapping
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S04 hash ledger, signature, and freshness validation contract
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S05 SQLite projection schema and rebuild policy
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S06 parser and projection implementation plan
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S07 parser/projection fixtures and expected-output ledgers
  + [slice_candidate] is IR2-S08 IR2 completion review and authority projection pack

  = must: keep IR2-S01 through IR2-S05 deeper-reasoning slices
  = must: route IR2-S06 to deeper reasoning if implementation plan changes authority, parser, projection, or storage semantics
  = should: route IR2-S07 to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark only after IR2-S01 through IR2-S06 are accepted and fixtures are bounded
  = must: route IR2-S08 to deeper reasoning because it accepts parser/projection implementation readiness and opens IR3
